The width- and ANSI-independence of the mutation classifier, re-run by the gate
host. Each of the two normalization operations is mutated independently and must
fail its own self-test; the restored classifier must pass.

$ sh -c bash specs/epic-195-a7-compatibility/verification/T-004/classifier-proof.sh
VIOLATE ANSI: remove escape-sequence stripping from the diagnostic classifier
CLASSIFIER-SELFTEST: ANSI or wrapped diagnostic did not match
ANSI_VIOLATED_EXIT_CODE=2
VIOLATE WRAP: remove newline compaction from the diagnostic classifier
CLASSIFIER-SELFTEST: ANSI or wrapped diagnostic did not match
WRAP_VIOLATED_EXIT_CODE=2
RESTORE: run the delivered ANSI/wrapped diagnostic classifier
CLASSIFIER-SELFTEST: ANSI and wrapped diagnostic matched
RESTORED_EXIT_CODE=0
CLASSIFIER-PROOF PASS: violation failed and restored classifier passed

exit status: 0
